Test that line numbers are correct during motion.

During program execution of non-motion commands, the status buffer is
updated from state tags stored in the interp queue.  While a motion is
playing out, stat should be updated from tags in the traj queue.

This test runs a program with a few short/quick moves followed by a
long, slow move.  The test watches axes, waiting until motion enters
the long move, and then checks that the line number reported by status
matches that of the program.
